From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erhan Bilgili <erhan.bilgili@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 5 Jul 2026 17:22:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 28/49] winewayland: Preserve GDI pixels above self-presenting
 children.

Punch-through compositing clears self-presenting child regions from the
parent window surface. This also clears GDI pixels from child windows
that are painted into the parent surface above those producers.

Track the server-computed region where GDI-only children cover producer
holes and publish the painted parent pixels as a small SHM producer.
Composite it above the producer content so those GDI pixels keep their
z-order.
